{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213575096,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b5c70635f41dc693","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"gh issue view 153"},"output":"title:\tRuling: delimit declarations explicitly\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t153\n--\nGrilled via docs/.grill/syntax-ergonomics.round.yaml, question record-argument-boundary (plans/language-oddities.md, issue #9's inventory).\n\n**Ruled: delimit declarations explicitly.** Replace the same-line heuristic (issues #10, #20) with a required terminator after every declaration -- the boundary becomes a token instead of a line-position fact.\n\n```toylang\nfn id(s: Str) -> Str = s;\n\n{a: 1}\n```\n\nImplementation: pick the terminator token (semicolon is the working example in the grill round; confirm during implementation it doesn't collide with anything else in the grammar), require it after every `fn` and `type` declaration, and retire the same-line same-line rule and its diagnostic once the terminator makes the ambiguity unreachable. Update the corpus-pinned test (record_body_after_definition) and docs/reference/syntax accordingly.\n","metadata":{"output":"title:\tRuling: delimit declarations explicitly\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tkantord (Dániel Kántor)\nlabels:\t\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t153\n--\nGrilled via docs/.grill/syntax-ergonomics.round.yaml, question record-argument-boundary (plans/language-oddities.md, issue #9's inventory).\n\n**Ruled: delimit declarations explicitly.** Replace the same-line heuristic (issues #10, #20) with a required terminator after every declaration -- the boundary becomes a token instead of a line-position fact.\n\n```toylang\nfn id(s: Str) -> Str = s;\n\n{a: 1}\n```\n\nImplementation: pick the terminator token (semicolon is the working example in the grill round; confirm during implementation it doesn't collide with anything else in the grammar), require it after every `fn` and `type` declaration, and retire the same-line same-line rule and its diagnostic once the terminator makes the ambiguity unreachable. Update the corpus-pinned test (record_body_after_definition) and docs/reference/syntax accordingly.\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"gh issue view 153","time":{"start":1788213575091,"end":1788213575094}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading AGENTS.md and the issue.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d5b94f001Eda2Gaa4iz9hkj","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d5a617001MR6tragE7FmPJR"}}
