{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213619323,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bb2373e0badbb0e2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/enum_recursive_walk.yaml"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/enum_recursive_walk.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Descending through the recursion rather than printing it: the arm's `.` is the nested\n2: # `Vec<Json>`, handed back to the same function. A variant arm compiles to the variant's\n3: # declaration index on the tagged backends, and that index was read off the placeholder before\n4: # kantord/toylang#94 -- Go panicked outright, Rust emitted a match over an empty arm list.\n5: #\n6: # Self-recursion rather than a `total`/`sum` pair, because jq's `def` has no forward declaration\n7: # and refuses a cycle between two named functions.\n8: program: |\n9:   enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\n10: \n11:   fn total(v: Vec<Json>) -> Int =\n12:       0 if length(v) == 0\n13:       else (v[0]! | arr -> total(.) or num -> .) + total(tail(v)!);\n14: \n15:   total([Json.arr([Json.num(1), Json.arr([Json.num(2), Json.num(3)])]), Json.num(4)])\n16: \n17: output: |\n18:   10\n19: \n20: node_types: [application, arith.add, builtin.length, builtin.tail, compare.eq, conditional, int, local, match, pipe, selection.collapse, unwrap, var, variant.payload, vec-literal]\n\n(End of file - total 20 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Descending through the recursion rather than printing it: the arm's `.` is the nested\n# `Vec<Json>`, handed back to the same function. A variant arm compiles to the variant's\n# declaration index on the tagged backends, and that index was read off the placeholder before\n# kantord/toylang#94 -- Go panicked outright, Rust emitted a match over an empty arm list.\n#\n# Self-recursion rather than a `total`/`sum` pair, because jq's `def` has no forward declaration\n# and refuses a cycle between two named functions.\nprogram: |\n  enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\n\n  fn total(v: Vec<Json>) -> Int =\n      0 if length(v) == 0\n      else (v[0]! | arr -> total(.) or num -> .) + total(tail(v)!);\n\n  total([Json.arr([Json.num(1), Json.arr([Json.num(2), Json.num(3)])]), Json.num(4)])\n\noutput: |\n  10\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, builtin.length, builtin.tail, compare.eq, conditional, int, local, match, pipe, selection.collapse, unwrap, var, variant.payload, vec-literal]","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/corpus/enum_recursive_walk.yaml","text":"# Descending through the recursion rather than printing it: the arm's `.` is the nested\n# `Vec<Json>`, handed back to the same function. A variant arm compiles to the variant's\n# declaration index on the tagged backends, and that index was read off the placeholder before\n# kantord/toylang#94 -- Go panicked outright, Rust emitted a match over an empty arm list.\n#\n# Self-recursion rather than a `total`/`sum` pair, because jq's `def` has no forward declaration\n# and refuses a cycle between two named functions.\nprogram: |\n  enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\n\n  fn total(v: Vec<Json>) -> Int =\n      0 if length(v) == 0\n      else (v[0]! | arr -> total(.) or num -> .) + total(tail(v)!);\n\n  total([Json.arr([Json.num(1), Json.arr([Json.num(2), Json.num(3)])]), Json.num(4)])\n\noutput: |\n  10\n\nnode_types: [application, arith.add, builtin.length, builtin.tail, compare.eq, conditional, int, local, match, pipe, selection.collapse, unwrap, var, variant.payload, vec-literal]","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":20,"totalLines":20,"truncated":false}},"title":"tests/corpus/enum_recursive_walk.yaml","time":{"start":1788213619311,"end":1788213619320}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This test needs semicolons. `fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \"arr\" or num -> \"num\"` needs a trailing `;`. Let me check the emit_toylang.rs to confirm the terminator is `;`. Yes, the issue says semicolon.\n\nI need to add `;` after the `enum Json {...}` declaration and after `fn describe(...) ... \"num\"`.\n\nLet me check what the format for declarations should look like - is it `enum Json { ... };` or does the `;` go after the closing brace? And for fn, after the body `= expr;`.\n\nLet me check the corpus files to see the established pattern.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d669630012yM4x3ZpAXqAn0","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d65ed2001G00KQdTG3gseOz"}}
