{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213630465,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b38fc6064cbc424","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"semicolon|Terminator|Semi|terminator\" src/parse.rs | head -40"},"output":"77:    Semicolon,\n123:            Tok::Semicolon => \"`;`\",\n249:        ';' => single(input, Tok::Semicolon),\n491:    /// `fn name(param: Type) -> Type = body;` or `fn name() -> Type = body;`. The terminator\n537:        self.eat(Tok::Semicolon)?;\n709:        self.eat(Tok::Semicolon)?;\n","metadata":{"output":"77:    Semicolon,\n123:            Tok::Semicolon => \"`;`\",\n249:        ';' => single(input, Tok::Semicolon),\n491:    /// `fn name(param: Type) -> Type = body;` or `fn name() -> Type = body;`. The terminator\n537:        self.eat(Tok::Semicolon)?;\n709:        self.eat(Tok::Semicolon)?;\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"rg -n \"semicolon|Terminator|Semi|terminator\" src/parse.rs | head -40","time":{"start":1788213630461,"end":1788213630463}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So the pattern in the corpus is `enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }` with NO semicolon after the enum? Wait, let me check enum_recursive_walk.yaml line 9: `enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }` - no trailing semicolon. But that corpus test passed (it's a corpus agreement test). Hmm.\n\nWait, but the corpus tests passed. Let me reconsider. Actually the enum declarations in corpus have no `;`. But those corpus files are pinned programs run at runtime, and they passed. So maybe `;` after enum is optional? Or maybe enum terminators are different from fn?\n\nWait, let me look more carefully. In enum_recursive_walk.yaml:\n```\nenum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\n\nfn total(v: Vec<Json>) -> Int =\n    0 if length(v) == 0\n    else (v[0]! | arr -> total(.) or num -> .) + total(tail(v)!);\n\ntotal(...)\n```\n\nThe enum has no `;` but the fn has `;`. And this test passed. So perhaps the parser doesn't require `;` after an enum when it's followed by a blank line / the next token is unambiguous? Or maybe enum doesn't require a terminator but fn does?\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read the failing test. The failing test has BOTH the enum and fn on a single logical string. The enum `enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }` is followed by blank line then `fn describe...`. And `fn describe(...) = \"num\"` is followed by blank line then `describe(...)`.\n\nIn the corpus that passed, the enum is followed by blank line then `fn`, and it worked without a `;`. But in the failing test, why did it fail? \n\nHmm, maybe the difference: in the corpus, after the fn's body there's `;` (total fn has `;`). In the failing test, the fn `describe` body ends with `\"num\"` with no `;`. So the missing `;` is after the fn declaration body, not the enum!\n\nWait but the enum in corpus also has no `;`. Let me think about the parser. Maybe enum terminator is optional because the closing brace `}` already disambiguates. But fn needs a `;` because the body is an expression that continues until the next declaration.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The failing test's fn `describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \"arr\" or num -> \"num\"` — the body ends with `\"num\"` and no `;`. Then the next line is `describe(Json.arr(...))` which is a call. Without a `;`, the parser might treat `\"num\"` then `describe(...)` ambiguously, OR the missing semicolon causes the parser to try to continue parsing.\n\nSo the fix for the failing test is to add `;` after the `describe` fn body. And possibly after the enum too. Let me check whether enum needs it.\n\nActually, let me look at how the parser requires it. Let me check what the prior run did to the corpus files. In enum_recursive_walk.yaml the enum has no semicolon. Let me check a corpus file that has fn where prior run added `;`.\n\nActually, the key question: does the failing test need `;` after the enum too? Let me look at the parse.rs to understand the terminator requirement. Let me search.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d6942200176rhRoNjzhcTCJ","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d66d8c001FeUeGo123xnGKi"}}
