{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213637959,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9dadd972a0b8d1cc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs","oldString":"             \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\"\\n\\n\\\n             describe(Json.arr([Json.num(1)]))\"","newString":"             \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\";\\n\\n\\\n             describe(Json.arr([Json.num(1)]))\""},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n@@ -71,10 +71,10 @@\n #[test]\n fn a_vec_wrapped_self_reference_typechecks() {\n     assert!(\n         toylang::compile(\n-            \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n-             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\"\\n\\n\\\n+             \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n+             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\";\\n\\n\\\n              describe(Json.arr([Json.num(1)]))\"\n         )\n         .is_ok()\n     );\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/tests/enums.rs\n@@ -71,10 +71,10 @@\n #[test]\n fn a_vec_wrapped_self_reference_typechecks() {\n     assert!(\n         toylang::compile(\n-            \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n-             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\"\\n\\n\\\n+             \"enum Json { arr(Vec<Json>), num(Int) }\\n\\n\\\n+             fn describe(j: Json) -> Str = j | arr -> \\\"arr\\\" or num -> \\\"num\\\";\\n\\n\\\n              describe(Json.arr([Json.num(1)]))\"\n         )\n         .is_ok()\n     );\n","additions":2,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"tests/enums.rs","time":{"start":1788213637956,"end":1788213637958}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"So `fn` requires a `;` (line 537), `type` alias requires `;` (line 709), but the enum declaration does NOT require a `;` — it ends at the closing brace (line 693). So enums are delimited by their closing brace naturally, no semicolon needed.\n\nWait, but the issue says \"require it after every `fn` and `type` declaration\". Enums are not in the list — only fn and type. So enums don't need a `;`. That's consistent with the corpus files (enum without `;` passed).\n\nSo the failing test only needs `;` after the `fn describe` body. The enum `enum Json {...}` doesn't need one.\n\nLet me verify: the failing test's fn body is `j | arr -> \"arr\" or num -> \"num\"` — ends with `\"num\"`, no `;`. Then next `describe(...)`. That's the issue.\n\nSo I fix the test to add `;` after the describe body. Let me update line 76.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d6ae8c001tIMnDAaidGpxTS","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d6a155001Yq74kb4V0xwFKk"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788213637984,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"id":"prt_059d6ad22001mMUc5cE3DWQoPx","messageID":"msg_059d6a155001Yq74kb4V0xwFKk","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","type":"text","text":"Enums are delimited by their closing brace (no `;`); only `fn` and `type` require the terminator. The failing test's `describe` fn body is missing the `;`. Fixing:\n\n","time":{"start":1788213636386,"end":1788213637978}}}
