{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213718554,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b8e0d6dd4d033957","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md","newString":"A program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\nprints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\nbecause the program is the expression. Each declaration ends with `;`, which is what separates\nit from the next declaration and from the program's own body.\n\n```toylang\n# Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\ntype Pair = {a: Int, b: Int};\n\nfn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b;\n\n{sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n```","oldString":"A program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\nprints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\nbecause the program is the expression.\n\n```toylang\n# Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\ntype Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n\nfn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n\n{sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n```"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n@@ -1,15 +1,16 @@\n # A program\n \n A program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\n prints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\n-because the program is the expression.\n+because the program is the expression. Each declaration ends with `;`, which is what separates\n+it from the next declaration and from the program's own body.\n \n ```toylang\n # Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\n-type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n+type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int};\n \n-fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n+fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b;\n \n {sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n ```\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/syntax/programs.md\n@@ -1,15 +1,16 @@\n # A program\n \n A program is declarations followed by one expression, and the expression's value is what\n prints. There are no statements, no `main`, and no print call: output needs no side effect,\n-because the program is the expression.\n+because the program is the expression. Each declaration ends with `;`, which is what separates\n+it from the next declaration and from the program's own body.\n \n ```toylang\n # Comments start with `#` and run to the end of the line.\n-type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}\n+type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int};\n \n-fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b\n+fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b;\n \n {sum: total({a: 1, b: 2})}\n ```\n \n","additions":4,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"docs/reference/syntax/programs.md","time":{"start":1788213718549,"end":1788213718552}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"This fragment uses a `type` alias and `fn`, both needing `;`. Let me update it. It's a syntax example; no `# fmt:` marker but the test skips non-parsing fragments anyway. Update:\n- Line 9: `type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int}` -> `type Pair = {a: Int, b: Int};`\n- Line 11: `fn total(p: Pair) -> Int = p.a + p.b` -> `... p.b;`\n\nAlso update the prose on line 3 to mention the terminator.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d7e5f7001RcKHI41DvFndYb","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d7de6d001gAABbJCG9MDW4R"}}
