{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213741356,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-aa6aef71b81033ee","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md","newString":"fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0];\n\nstr(head([1, 2, 3])!)","oldString":"fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0]\n\nstr(head([1, 2, 3])!)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n@@ -21,9 +21,9 @@\n `Opt` is in the type grammar, so a function may declare one as a parameter or return type,\n which is what lets it hand the absence back instead of being forced to insist:\n \n ```toylang\n-fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0]\n+fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0];\n \n str(head([1, 2, 3])!)\n ```\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/opt.md\n@@ -21,9 +21,9 @@\n `Opt` is in the type grammar, so a function may declare one as a parameter or return type,\n which is what lets it hand the absence back instead of being forced to insist:\n \n ```toylang\n-fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0]\n+fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0];\n \n str(head([1, 2, 3])!)\n ```\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"docs/reference/types/opt.md","time":{"start":1788213741353,"end":1788213741354}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"These are many fragments with fn declarations that need `;`. This is a lot of edits. Let me update each. The lines:\n- 25: `fn head(v: Vec<Int>) -> Opt<Int> = v[0]` -> `... v[0];`\n- 58: `fn shallow() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = some(none)` -> `... some(none);`\n- 70: `fn shallow() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = none` -> `... none;`\n- 95, 97, 99: `fn deep()... = some(some(7))` -> `;`, `fn shallow()... = some(none)` -> `;`, `fn absent()... = none` -> `;`\n\nLet me update each with edits. I'll do them.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d844a7001XLQIYgEpyTWMP9","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d83ad300130JvKZR9eB701G"}}
