absent-looking one and a value that is absent all the way down print\n identically:\n \n ```toylang\n-fn deep() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = some(some(7))\n+fn deep() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = some(some(7));\n \n-fn shallow() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = some(none)\n+fn shallow() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = some(none);\n \n-fn absent() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = none\n+fn absent() -> Opt<Opt<Int>> = none;\n \n {a: deep(), b: shallow(), c: absent()}\n ```\n \n","additions":3,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"docs/reference/types/opt.md","time":{"start":1788213746568,"end":1788213746571}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_059d857e3001RchJuG42r5vWY5","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d85482001k5afRnt1fb6BDS"}}
