:"The enum declarations don't need `;` (they end at closing brace). But the `fn area_ish(s: Shape) -> Int = s | circle{r} -> r * r` at line 37 needs `;`. Let me update it. The error message references byte offsets - those are snapshots of error messages. The error message at line 43 says \"missing `point` (at byte 73)\". The byte offsets in these error messages may now shift due to the `;` addition... wait, this error is from `area_ish(Shape.point)` where the missing `point` variant is reported. Adding `;` to line 37 would shift the byte offsets of subsequent content. Line 43's `(at byte 73)` would change.\n\nHmm, this is a problem. The error message byte offset is pinned. Let me check how these docs error fences are validated. In docs.rs, `Outcome::Error(want)` compares the compile error message to `want`. So the byte offset must match exactly.\n\nIf I add `;` to line 37, the byte offset of `point` in `area_ish(Shape.point)` shifts. Let me compute. Actually, this is getting complex. Let me check: is this enum.md fragment actually part of the test? It has an `error` fence. So yes.\n\nWait — but this is precisely the kind of byte-offset churn that the prior runs were handling with .snap files. For docs error fences, I need to manually update the byte offsets.\n\nLet me reconsider. Adding `;` after `area_ish` body: the text `fn area_ish(s: Shape) -> Int = s | circle{r} -> r * r` becomes `...r * r;`. That adds 1 char at position... Let me compute the byte offset of `point` in the program.\n\nThe program (with `;` added) is:\n```\nenum Shape { point, circle{r: Int} }\n\nfn area_ish(s: Shape) -> Int = s | circle{r} -> r * r;\n\narea_ish(Shape.point)\n```\n\nLet me count bytes. Actually, let me just run the program to see what error byte offset it produces after my edit. But first, let me make the edit and then run just check to find the actual offsets, then fix them.\n\nActually, a cleaner approach: make all the edits, then run `just check`, and for any doc error-fence offset failures, fix the offsets to match what the compiler now reports.\n\nLet me update enum.md line 37.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d88181001IkQjXj4tKL3eVZ","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d86255001tZr70SIpH5UXec"}}
