{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213784870,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-903a6072dc251765","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md","newString":"fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456;\n\nbig() + 1","oldString":"fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456\n\nbig() + 1"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n@@ -45,9 +45,9 @@\n A bare literal on either side of an `Int64` operator needs no bridge -- its position already\n says which width it has:\n \n ```toylang\n-fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456\n+fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456;\n \n big() + 1\n ```\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/int64.md\n@@ -45,9 +45,9 @@\n A bare literal on either side of an `Int64` operator needs no bridge -- its position already\n says which width it has:\n \n ```toylang\n-fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456\n+fn big() -> Int64 = 1234567890123456;\n \n big() + 1\n ```\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"docs/reference/types/int64.md","time":{"start":1788213784863,"end":1788213784868}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"pr