{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788213786169,"sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-882f951762d5436e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/stream.md"},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/stream.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Stream\n2: \n3: `Stream<T>`: effect-layer multiplicity\n4: ([ADR 0001](../../adr/0001-stream-is-the-effect-layer-typed.md)). The type says an\n5: expression yields its entries one at a time as evaluation proceeds, not that a stream object\n6: exists as a value.\n7: \n8: A stream is born only at a source -- [`inputs`](../sources/inputs.md) or\n9: [`lines`](../sources/lines.md) -- and dies at [`collect`](../builtins/collect.md) or at the\n10: [`jsonlines`](../builtins/jsonlines.md) sink. In between, `select`, `map`, and projection\n11: accept a `Stream` subject and yield a `Stream` back, so a whole pipeline can live in the\n12: effect layer:\n13: \n14: ```case\n15: lines_stream_signature\n16: ```\n17: \n18: The rules, each of which the checker enforces:\n19: \n20: - A stream is consumed exactly once; using one twice would read the same real stdin twice.\n21: - A stream never sits inside a record, a `Vec`, or another `Stream`.\n22: - A stream cannot be printed. It is not a value; `collect` is what makes one.\n23: - A function cannot conjure a stream: a signature may return `Stream` only if a `Stream`\n24:   came in through its parameter, so the pipeline stays one chain from source to sink.\n25: \n26: ```toylang\n27: fn conjure(n: Int) -> Stream<Int> = lines | map(n)\n28: \n29: 0\n30: ```\n31: \n32: ```error\n33: `conjure` returns Stream<Int> without taking a stream; a stream is born only at a source (at byte 0)\n34: ```\n35: \n36: What the chain buys is fusion: a pipeline of the right shape compiles to a read-one,\n37: transform-one, write-one loop on every backend, printing each entry before the next is read.\n38: `tests/streaming.rs` is what proves that; the corpus pins only the values.\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Stream\n\n`Stream<T>`: effect-layer multiplicity\n([ADR 0001](../../adr/0001-stream-is-the-effect-layer-typed.md)). The type says an\nexpression yields its entries one at a time as evaluation proceeds, not that a stream object\nexists as a value.\n\nA stream is born only at a source -- [`inputs`](../sources/inputs.md) or\n[`lines`](../sources/lines.md) -- and dies at [`collect`](../builtins/collect.md) or at the\n[`jsonlines`](../builtins/jsonlines.md) sink. In between, `select`, `map`, and projection\naccept a `Stream` subject and yield a `Stream` back, so a whole pipeline can live in the\neffect layer:\n\n```case\nlines_stream_signature\n```\n\nThe rules, each of which the checker enforces:\n\n- A stream is consumed exactly once; using one twice would read the same real stdin twice.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-153/docs/reference/types/stream.md","text":"# Stream\n\n`Stream<T>`: effect-layer multiplicity\n([ADR 0001](../../adr/0001-stream-is-the-effect-layer-typed.md)). The type says an\nexpression yields its entries one at a time as evaluation proceeds, not that a stream object\nexists as a value.\n\nA stream is born only at a source -- [`inputs`](../sources/inputs.md) or\n[`lines`](../sources/lines.md) -- and dies at [`collect`](../builtins/collect.md) or at the\n[`jsonlines`](../builtins/jsonlines.md) sink. In between, `select`, `map`, and projection\naccept a `Stream` subject and yield a `Stream` back, so a whole pipeline can live in the\neffect layer:\n\n```case\nlines_stream_signature\n```\n\nThe rules, each of which the checker enforces:\n\n- A stream is consumed exactly once; using one twice would read the same real stdin twice.\n- A stream never sits inside a record, a `Vec`, or another `Stream`.\n- A stream cannot be printed. It is not a value; `collect` is what makes one.\n- A function cannot conjure a stream: a signature may return `Stream` only if a `Stream`\n  came in through its parameter, so the pipeline stays one chain from source to sink.\n\n```toylang\nfn conjure(n: Int) -> Stream<Int> = lines | map(n)\n\n0\n```\n\n```error\n`conjure` returns Stream<Int> without taking a stream; a stream is born only at a source (at byte 0)\n```\n\nWhat the chain buys is fusion: a pipeline of the right shape compiles to a read-one,\ntransform-one, write-one loop on every backend, printing each entry before the next is read.\n`tests/streaming.rs` is what proves that; the corpus pins only the values.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":38,"totalLines":38,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/reference/types/stream.md","time":{"start":1788213786163,"end":1788213786167}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_059d8f539001HTKo4J6uacfjVL","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d8f145001BflZbtW8X7QQss"}}
