ss runs ALL toylang fences regardless. Wait, but the `syntax-example` fragments in functions.md had `# fmt: syntax-example` marker. That marker is for the fmt_examples test only. The docs.rs harness runs all toylang fences and requires output/refuses/error fences.\n\nWait, functions.md fragments had `output: 42` fences. So they're run. Good, I updated them.\n\nNow these other files (tutorial, guides, builtins) have fn/type declarations too. If they have output/error fences, they'll fail now without `;`. I need to update all of them.\n\nThis is a large mechanical change across many docs files. Let me be systematic. Let me grep for all `fn`/`type` declaration lines across docs and update each. But I must also fix any byte offsets in error fences.\n\nGiven the volume, let me use a strategy: update all fn/type declaration fences, then run the docs test to catch offset mismatches, then fix those.\n\nLet me look at each file's declaration lines and whether they have error fences with offsets. Let me grep for the fn/type lines across all these files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_059d957db001Ymo10rfNScGtGb","sessionID":"ses_fa62a5b39ffevmxUbcy053FMKH","messageID":"msg_059d946fd001h1zktZEPcmVWHh"}}
